2026-08-27: Read the four provided Geneid/count tables; all had 7,127 unique IDs in identical order.
Design: changed = SRR5085169, SRR5085170; reference = SRR5085167, SRR5085168; contrast = changed vs reference.
Prefilter: retained rows with raw count >=10 in at least 2 of 4 samples; 2,526 genes retained.
Method: DESeq2 Wald test on the retained raw-count matrix; unshrunken log2 fold changes; reference level set to reference.
DESeq2 result options: independent filtering disabled and Cook's outlier filtering disabled so every retained gene was tested and reported.
Validation: 2,526 output rows; exact four-column header; IDs/order match the prefiltered input universe; all log2 fold changes finite; p-values and FDRs in [0,1]; FDR agrees with BH over 2,526 p-values.
